[{"id":"serial-number-dispute-procedure-00","source":"serial-number-dispute-procedure.txt","index":0,"section":"DUCKS ON THE POND CARDS SERIAL-NUMBER DISPUTE PROCEDURE","sections":["DUCKS ON THE POND CARDS SERIAL-NUMBER DISPUTE PROCEDURE","1. WHY SERIAL NUMBERS ARE PROTECTED","2. WHAT IS AND IS NOT A CONFLICT","3. COMMON CAUSES","4. WHAT TO DO AS A COLLECTOR","4. WHAT TO DO AS A COLLECTOR › 4.1 Before you add the card"],"words":371,"overlapWords":0,"text":"DUCKS ON THE POND CARDS SERIAL-NUMBER DISPUTE PROCEDURE\n\nVersion: 1.0 DRAFT, November 2026 Owner: Ducks on the Pond Cards support team Applies to: collectors who record numbered cards, and the admins who review serial-number conflicts.\n\nThis procedure expands on section 6.6 and section 10 of the User's Guide (users-guide.txt) and section 7 of the Customer Service Policy (customer-service-policy.txt). If they ever disagree, the Customer Service Policy applies. Items marked [TO CONFIRM] are placeholders.\n\n1. WHY SERIAL NUMBERS ARE PROTECTED\n\nA numbered card is one of a limited print run, for example 23/50. Only one physical card carries serial 23 of that variant. To keep the records honest, the Application allows only one unsold copy of a variant to hold a given serial number across all collections.\n\nSold copies do not count. If a collector marks serial 23 as sold, another collector can then record serial 23 of that variant without a conflict.\n\n2. WHAT IS AND IS NOT A CONFLICT\n\nNot a conflict (rejected straight away, with a message):\n\n- The serial is higher than the print run. \"Serial N is higher than the print run (/M).\" - You already hold that serial of that variant yourself. \"You already have serial N of this card.\" - The cert number is already recorded for that grading company. \"That already exists.\"\n\nA conflict (sent to an admin):\n\n- Another collector's unsold copy of the same variant already holds the serial. You see: \"Serial #N is already in another collection, so this was sent to an admin for review.\"\n\nThe same serial on a different variant is not a conflict. Serial 23 of the Gold Refractor and serial 23 of the Orange Refractor are different cards.\n\n3. COMMON CAUSES\n\nFrom most to least common [TO CONFIRM once there is real data]:\n\n1. A typo: one collector entered the wrong serial. 2. The wrong variant: the card was recorded under the wrong parallel, so it collides with someone else's card. 3. A stale record: the card was sold or traded outside the Application, and the previous owner never marked it sold. 4. A duplicate catalog entry: the same parallel was added twice. 5. A counterfeit or altered card.\n\n4. WHAT TO DO AS A COLLECTOR","tokens":497,"embedding":[-0.08685707300901413,0.03726423159241676,-0.034256115555763245,-0.03240472078323364,0.025374548509716988,0.03945377469062805,0.06004643067717552,0.041853781789541245,0.06723536550998688,0.009379944764077663,0.04101286083459854,0.022023603320121765,0.05952626094222069,-0.05161195248365402,-0.04388582333922386,-0.05091722682118416,-0.06356487423181534,-0.0398813858628273,-0.06437670439481735,0.038021061569452286,0.021633842960000038,-0.013446968980133533,-0.034518808126449585,0.06558848917484283,-0.08219879120588303,-0.018601717427372932,-0.08588622510433197,0.04958615452051163,-0.04501362517476082,-0.031057065352797508,-0.028665529564023018,0.12861888110637665,0.033173561096191406,0.03216811642050743,-0.0008244722266681492,-0.06709586828947067,-0.02502594329416752,0.009017623960971832,0.04379161074757576,-0.05174803361296654,-0.01212710328400135,-0.011908039450645447,-0.038576893508434296,0.011203300207853317,-0.038869671523571014,-0.010606152005493641,-0.08031995594501495,0.031759850680828094,-0.11261677742004395,0.05180314928293228,-0.0655597448348999,0.02164347656071186,-0.024807661771774292,0.0596274770796299,0.04928087070584297,0.02283582277595997,0.0006610635900869966,-0.03582732379436493,-0.03167109936475754,-0.04205606132745743,0.018219444900751114,-0.002294539473950863,-