82246422768,-0.018256038427352905,0.019249465316534042,-0.07066896557807922,0.020233485847711563,-0.021883992478251457,0.04969710856676102,0.029418474063277245,0.026052972301840782,0.034706100821495056,0.014420070685446262,-0.0025722982827574015,0.002383197657763958,-0.043519698083400726,-0.08505254238843918,0.02960732951760292,0.12827065587043762,0.002693318296223879,-0.09299379587173462,-0.07651588320732117,-0.053609635680913925,-0.0171465165913105,-0.06283155083656311,-0.020140238106250763,0.06027873605489731,0.06452593952417374,-0.01946699619293213,-0.0021356281358748674,0.0271290373057127,-0.021513938903808594,0.022498901933431625,-0.021938705816864967,0.1319071650505066,0.015645531937479973,0.046053387224674225,0.09316431730985641]},{"id":"serial-number-dispute-procedure-01","source":"serial-number-dispute-procedure.txt","index":1,"section":"4. WHAT TO DO AS A COLLECTOR › 4.1 Before you add the card","sections":["4. WHAT TO DO AS A COLLECTOR › 4.1 Before you add the card","4. WHAT TO DO AS A COLLECTOR › 4.2 When the conflict message appears","4. WHAT TO DO AS A COLLECTOR › 4.3 While you wait","4. WHAT TO DO AS A COLLECTOR › 4.4 After the decision","5. EVIDENCE","5. EVIDENCE › 5.1 What we may ask for","5. EVIDENCE › 5.2 How strong each kind of evidence is","6. HOW AN ADMIN REVIEWS A CONFLICT","6. HOW AN ADMIN REVIEWS A CONFLICT › 6.1 The queue"],"words":388,"overlapWords":0,"text":"4.1 Before you add the card\n\n- Check the serial against the card itself, not a listing or a photo. - Check you chose the right set, card and parallel. - For a graded card, have the cert number ready.\n\n4.2 When the conflict message appears\n\nYour card is not lost. It is waiting for review. Use the \"Note for admin\" box to explain, for example:\n\n\"Card is in hand, PSA cert 12345678. Bought from a card show on 2026-10-12. The other entry may be a typo.\"\n\nAdd the note when you add the card. There is no way to add or change it after the card has been submitted.\n\n4.3 While you wait\n\n- Track the review under \"My serial-number reviews\" at the bottom of My collection. Statuses are \"pending admin review\", \"approved\" and \"rejected\". - Watch for a support email asking for evidence (section 5). Email notifications from the Application are not available yet, so check My collection for updates. - If you sold or traded away the other copy yourself, under another account, tell support.\n\n4.4 After the decision\n\n- Approved: the card is added to your collection with the details you submitted. It starts not tradeable. - Rejected: the card is not added. Read the admin's note to see why. - If you disagree, ask for a second review (section 8).\n\n5. EVIDENCE\n\n5.1 What we may ask for\n\n- A clear photo of the front and back of the card showing the serial number. - For a graded card, the grading company and cert number, and a photo of the slab label. - Proof of purchase or trade, if you have it (a receipt, invoice or message).\n\nCrop or cover any personal details such as an address label before you send a photo. We will never ask for a password, payment card number or bank detail.\n\n5.2 How strong each kind of evidence is\n\nStrongest A grading company cert whose record shows the serial number. We check the cert on the grading company's own website. Strong Clear photos of the front and back that show the serial and match the catalog entry. Supporting Receipts, invoices or messages showing when and where the card was bought. Weak Photos from a listing, or a description with no photo.\n\n6. HOW AN ADMIN REVIEWS A CONFLICT","tokens":505,"embedding":[-0.11143245548009872,0.08057355135679245,-0.0669480711221695,-0.023831937462091446,0.04536353051662445,0.0321405865252018,0.01215325202792883,0.04800540953874588,0.04958869144320488,0.018671466037631035,0.06522387266159058,-0.005197355058044195,0.044871021062135696,-0.05636102706193924,-0.056581441313028336,-0.06459410488605499,0.013225977309048176,-0.01695186458528042,-0.06694122403860092,0.08412