 decision","6. HOW AN ADMIN REVIEWS A CONFLICT › 6.4 Target times","7. DECISION RULES"],"words":275,"overlapWords":0,"text":"6.1 The queue\n\nOpen the Admin page (admins only). It shows the 50 most recent conflicts, open ones first. Each shows the variant, the serial, who submitted it and when, their note and copy details, and the existing copy and its owner.\n\n6.2 Steps\n\n1. Read both entries side by side. Check the variant, serial, grade and cert number of each. 2. Look for an obvious recording mistake: a typo, the wrong parallel, or a duplicate catalog entry. 3. If it is not obvious, contact both collectors for evidence (section 5). 4. Wait up to 14 days for replies. If a collector does not reply in that time, decide on the evidence you have. 5. Decide (section 7) and record it. 6. Write a note the collector will understand. Every decision records who resolved it and when.\n\n6.3 Recording the decision\n\nTo approve the new submission, first free the serial:\n\n- \"Change existing copy's serial to\" a corrected number, then \"Save\"; or - \"Delete existing copy\", if it should not exist at all.\n\nThen enter a note and click \"Approve\". If the serial is still held you will see: \"Serial N is still held by a copy. Fix or delete that copy first.\"\n\nTo keep the existing copy, enter a note and click \"Reject\".\n\nNever change or delete another collector's copy without a clear reason written in the note.\n\n6.4 Target times\n\n- First review: within 5 business days of submission. - Waiting for evidence: up to 14 days. - Second review: a reply within 10 business days of the request.\n\n7. DECISION RULES\n\nSituation Decision ------------------------------------------ ---------------------------------- The new entry is a typo Reject.","tokens":440,"embedding":[-0.10793603211641312,0.0362253338098526,-0.014070426113903522,-0.028696145862340927,-0.004346814472228289,-0.017399633303284645,-0.03820843622088432,-0.011638175696134567,0.06429138034582138,0.04432776570320