S","8. SECOND REVIEW AND COMPLAINTS","9. KNOWN LIMITS"],"words":300,"overlapWords":11,"text":"Situation Decision ------------------------------------------ ---------------------------------- The new entry is a typo Reject.\n\nNote the likely correct serial so the collector can re-add The existing entry is a typo Correct the existing serial, then approve Wrong variant on one side Reject that side, with a note to re-add under the right variant The existing owner no longer has the card Delete the existing copy (or ask its owner to mark it sold), then approve Both claim the card; one has a cert that Decide for the cert holder records the serial Both have equal evidence Keep the existing copy, reject, and explain; either may ask for a second review No evidence from either side after 14 days Keep the existing copy, reject Signs of a counterfeit or altered card Reject, and refer to the acceptable-use rules (Customer Service Policy section 9)\n\nDeliberately entering a serial you do not hold, to block another collector, breaks the Terms of Use (section 9) and can lead to the account being restricted or closed.\n\n8. SECOND REVIEW AND COMPLAINTS\n\nIf you disagree with a decision:\n\n1. Reply to your support conversation, or contact support, and ask for a second review. Include any new evidence. 2. An admin who did not make the first decision reviews it and replies within 10 business days. 3. If you are still unhappy, follow the complaints steps in section 11 of the Customer Service Policy. The support lead's decision is final.\n\nAn admin decision settles the Application's records. It does not decide who legally owns a physical card.\n\n9. KNOWN LIMITS\n\n- No email notifications for submitters or admins yet. - The \"Note for admin\" cannot be edited after submission. - A copy's serial can only be changed by an admin. - The queue shows the 50 most recent conflicts only.","tokens":442,"embedding":[-0.10526397824287415,0.06923361122608185,0.0003921869501937181,-0.017816187813